  "idea": "CapCut vs Premiere Pro: is professional editing software still necessary",
  "text": "Premiere Pro vs CapCut: which video editor actually gives you the fastest turnaround time? Trying to edit thirty vertical videos monthly inside Premiere causes constant cache clearing and dropped preview frames. The legacy NLE architecture was never built for rapid mobile aspect ratios and short-form pacing. CapCut streamlines production with hardware-accelerated scrubbing, instant B-roll insertion, and automated subtitle styling. This saves you twenty production hours weekly.",
